  "about": "Run outcomes for one mutable or append-only stream after a base of three records (a, b, z). producer and intake are what each side does to the stream's other-device copy: replace (drop what the run omits) or merge (same-key merge only). Intake sees: outcome, collection, timeRange, semantics, records, skippedDelete, oversize, covered, retainedState (incremental runs: whether a cursor was saved). The desktop producer sees: mode, collection, timeRange, retainedState, semantics, records, skippedDelete, detailGap, proof. proof says what the producer's completion proof is built from: matching (the run's own records), mismatched (other records), none (no reviewed completion contract). The completion proof, and a record too large for the writer, reach only one side. producerOnly marks a case where the two sides cannot see the same input. safe=false marks a case where intake replaces and the producer merges. Both sides' decisions are asserted by their tests; a change to any value must change the hash in both tests.",
